cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PLCSEC in research, cite this software release and include the exact version and capture-analysis scope. Do not include sensitive operational data in citations."
title: "PLCSEC: Industrial Controller Security Assessment Framework"
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-11-23
type: software
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  PLCSEC is a safety-first Python framework for passive industrial control
  system protocol analysis, OT asset inventory reconciliation, site-profile
  review, baseline drift, Ed25519-signed evidence and approvals, bounded
  offline firmware container metadata inspection, offline OPC UA application
  certificate path review, read-only identity checks, STIX/CEF integration,
  DNP3 CRC validation, offline advisory correlation and a signed-checkpoint-
  capable evidence ledger.
keywords:
  - operational technology
  - industrial control systems
  - PLC security
  - passive network analysis
  - Modbus TCP
  - S7comm
  - EtherNet/IP
  - OPC UA
  - firmware analysis
  - Ed25519
  - signed evidence
